M162","status":"active"},{"type":"course","code":"AN N EA M170","status":"active"},{"type":"course","code":"ENGL 111A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"ENGL 111C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GERMAN 109","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"HIST C191F","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"IRANIAN 130","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"IRANIAN 131","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"IRANIAN 132","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"IRANIAN M178","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"POL SCI 132A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"POL SCI M132B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"SEMITIC 130","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"RELIGN 120","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 101A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 101B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 101C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 102A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 102B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 102C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 121A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 121B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 121C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 130","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 131A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 131B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"YIDDSH 131C","status":"inactive"}],"label":"Recommended Elective"}],"count":6,"label":"Electives","notes":"Select six upper-division elective courses from Hebrew subject area or Jewish studies subject area or from the following list:"}],"label":"The Major"}}],"narrative":[],"overrides_applied":[]},"nodes":[{"id":"AN N EA 10W","title":"Jerusalem: Holy City","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Elective"],"column":1,"prereq_text":"English Composition 3","requires":{"type":"course","code":"ENGCOMP 3","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Not open for credit to students with credit for course 10. Survey of religious, political, and cultural history of Jerusalem over three millennia as symbolic focus of three faiths: Judaism, Christianity, and Islam. Transformation of sacred space as reflected by literary and archaeological evidence through examination of testimony of artifacts, architecture, and iconography in relation to written word. Study of creation of mythic Jerusalem through event and experience. Satisfies Writing II requirement. Letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ANNEA10W"},{"id":"AN N EA M135","title":"Religion in Ancient Israel","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["The Major: Recommended Elective"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"(Same as Religion M135.) Lecture, three hours. Introductory survey of various ancient Israelite religious beliefs and practices, their origin, and development, with special attention to diversity of religious practice in ancient Israel and Canaan during 1st millennium BCE. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ANNEAM135"},{"id":"AN N EA M162","title":"Archaeology, Identity, and Bible","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["The Major: Recommended Elective"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"(Formerly numbered 162.) (Same as Jewish Studies M165.) Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Introduction of archaeological record of southern Levant (ancient Israel) from Bronze Age through Achaemenid Period (circa 2500 to 332 BC) in combination with current understandings of genre, authorship, and historical value of Hebrew Bible. Ancient Israelite identities are traced through combination of archaeological and textual sources. Social, religious, and political traditions of ancient Israel and Judah are interpreted in context of both earlier Bronze Age traditions and Israel’s Iron Age neighbors. Archaeological and textual data for identities, such as Amorites, Canaanites, Phoenicians, Egyptians, Assyrians, and Babylonians, form basis for evaluating construction and maintenance of various biblical identities. Introduction to theoretical and methodological issues involving historical archaeology of ancient Israel and Levant, and possibilities for investigating negotiation of identity in archaeological record. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ANNEAM162"},{"id":"AN N EA M170","title":"Bible and Its Interpreters","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["The Major: Recommended Elective"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"(Same as Religion M172.) Lecture, three hours. Knowledge of original languages not required. Bible (Old and New Testaments) as book. Canon, text, and versions. Linguistic, literary, historical, and religious approaches to Bible study. Survey of history of interpretation from antiquity to present. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ANNEAM170"},{"id":"ARABIC 1A","title":"Elementary Standard Arabic","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":false,"role":"prerequisite","groups":[],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, six hours. Course 1A is enforced Not open to students with prior knowledge of Arabic. Introduction to formal Arabic (modern standard Arabic), including listening, speaking, reading, and writing. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ARABIC1A"},{"id":"ARABIC 1B","title":"Elementary Standard Arabic","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":false,"role":"prerequisite","groups":[],"column":1,"prereq_text":"course 1A","requires":{"type":"course","code":"ARABIC 1A","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, six hours. Not open to students with prior knowledge of Arabic. Introduction to formal Arabic (modern standard Arabic), including listening, speaking, reading, and writing. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ARABIC1B"},{"id":"ARABIC 1C","title":"Elementary Standard Arabic","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Foreign Language"],"column":2,"prereq_text":"course 1B","requires":{"type":"course","code":"ARABIC 1B","concurrent":false,"min_grade":null},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, six hours. Not open to students with prior knowledge of Arabic. Introduction to formal Arabic (modern standard Arabic), including listening, speaking, reading, and writing. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ARABIC1C"},{"id":"ARMENIA 101C","title":"Elementary Modern Western Armenian","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Foreign Language"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, five hours. Students with knowledge of Armenian should contact instructor to determine appropriate enrollment level. Armenian grammar, conversation, and exercises. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/ARMENIA101C"},{"id":"ARMENIA 104C","title":"Elementary Modern Eastern Armenian","units":"5","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"required","gr